# subalpine_fir_floor_b: a pair of subalpine firs far below, on a basin's
# floor (BUILD_PLAN S5 brief B9), drawn at floor scale for the wide pixel
# (11.2): two spires 4 and 3 rows tall, each one column wide at the tip
# and stepping out a column at a time to its foot, a column of floor
# between their feet; shadow side spruce (11) on the left and lit side
# forest (12) on the right, as subalpine_fir_floor_a's. No trunks. The
# anchor, 0,0, is the taller spire's foot. 7 wide, 4 tall.
C 11  L 0,-3 0,0  L -1,0
C 12  L 1,-2 1,0
C 11  L 4,-2 4,0  L 3,0
C 12  L 5,-1 5,0
